•fauthorxApub:sha2-256:m2smuezcqpjeyy6iofa2pjl47lgbwu254hohndyhs2do34fcrcmadbodyßeclassharchivalgcontentxtpublet-cli 0.2.0 was released on 2026-10-09 from commit 7d6d6ef4d9e0a77387d0f444d16e3d9dba07b613 with these changes.ddata¢gcolumnsÇ°dnamehcategory°dnamefchangedrowsèÇhinternalx÷graphset's code moved into the workspace as the publet-algorithms crate, and publet-merkle's re-exports were replaced by it; nothing pub does changed (every scenario passes, and the evaluation digest is unchanged).Çhinternalx˝The graph traversals (publet-graph's cycle check, depends closure, equivalence classes and lineage walks, and pub build's topological sort) and the delta checkpoint schedule now share one implementation in publet-algorithms; their results are unchanged.ÇhinternalxƒVersion requirement matching (^X.Y, X.Y+, prefixes) moved from pub render into publet-algorithms' version module, with Version parsing and bump arithmetic; pub render and pub env behave as before.Çhinternalxüpublet-core and publet-algorithms are released on version tracks of their own; publet-core's manifest states its version instead of inheriting the workspace's.ÇgchangedxóA render pipeline's tool requirement ^X.Y means what it means to Cargo: below 1.0 it admits only the same minor version (^0.1 admits 0.1.9, not 0.2.0).Çhinternalxöcargo-deny is stricter (0.20.2; unmaintained and unsound crates fail; crates.io only) and cargo-vet records supply-chain audits; nothing pub does changed.ÇhinternalxThe published crates' documentation is reworked; a guard checks every public function has an example. Nothing pub does changed.ÇhinternalxæTest vectors from independent sources, property tests, and two independent implementations as test oracles (ciborium for CBOR, ct-merkle for RFC 6962). Tests only; nothing users run changed.Çhsecurityyzpub compiles in three fixes found by fuzzing: the CBOR decoder no longer accepts null in a two-byte form (a second encoding and identifier for the same object), identifier parsing refuses non-zero base32 padding bits (many spellings of one identifier), and Merkle proof checking no longer loops forever, or panics (pub's release builds check overflow), on a log size above 2^63.ÇhinternalxjCI builds publet-core and publet-algorithms on their minimum Rust version, 1.85; nothing pub does changed.ÇhinternalxæEach change to the public API of publet-core and publet-algorithms is checked against the crate's last release by cargo-semver-checks, and the crate docs gain a Versioning section saying so.Çhinternalx+tree::Node's docs say why it is exhaustive.ÇhinternalxLThe log's absurd-size regression tests also build and run on 32-bit targets.Çhinternalx?publet-algorithms checks proofs with u64 sizes on every target.Çhinternalx®The crates' include patterns are anchored with /, so a file of the same name deeper in a crate can never be packaged by accident; each package's contents are unchanged.gdependsÅxApub:sha2-256:rbmwxy4zfiev2fsfbm742uz3jnzxczn2yojf32geu2hcbypipzpqhevidenceÅ§dkindhexternalcrefjpublet-clihrevisionx(7d6d6ef4d9e0a77387d0f444d16e3d9dba07b613drolefsourcedlangbenescope¢jconditionsÄfdomainx*the published release v0.2.0 of publet-cligcreatedt2026-10-09T00:00:00Zcpuba1dtypekclaim.prose